'''Raül Moragas''' (10 April 1944{{Spaced en dash}}18 February 2024) was a [[Balisca|Baliscan]] politician, who served as the xth [[Secretary General of Balisca]] from 1992 to 1998. During his political career, Moragas was a member of the [[Cosmopolitan Collective]] platform, representing the [[Alunzaro (commune district)|Alunzaro]] [[commune district]]. Moragas was the first Secretary General of [[Sugihan Baliscans|Sugihan]] descent.

His tenure was primarily defined by the challenge of reconciling Balisca's [[W:Libertarian socialism|libertarian socialist]] economic model within a rapidly changing global landscape, marked by the collapse of the [[W:Eastern Bloc|Eastern Bloc]] and the rise of a [[W:Unipolarity|unipolar]] world. Moragas's administration focused on economic resilience against [[Soviet Reformation|post-Soviet austerity]], strengthening economic ties with the [[W:Global South|Global South]], and sustaining Balisca's core ideological commitments amidst external pressures. He balanced the nation's ingrained [[decentralization]] with the pragmatic need for unified action to ensure stability and progress.

Under Moragas's leadership, Balisca pursued strategic regional economic integration, notably negotiating for membership in [[W:Mercosur|Mercosur]] as a counterbalance to perceived [[W:Neoliberalism|Western globalizing pressures]], along with aiding the Soviet Union's reformation and [[COCO#Post-Cold War activity|integration into COCO]]. Domestically, his administration prioritized sustaining Balisca's [[Social protection in Balisca|social protection system]] and managing the integration of a new wave of immigrant communities, spearheading the confederation's "[[W:No one is illegal|Nadie es ilegal]]" policy. 

